{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bkKTuQF6Vfb9zHaM9sAUn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form overall assessment scoring 1 2 3 4 5 scale 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review assessment scoring. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Review Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Overall Assessment Scale\n\nBased on the search results, the ACL Rolling Review uses a **1-5 scale** for the overall assessment scoring. The Overall Assessment descriptions include: 5.0 \"Award-worthy (top 2.5%)\" and 4.0 (the results appear to be truncated, but indicate there is a five-point scale).\n\n## Key Requirements\n\n- The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n- If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\nThe search results show that this scoring system has been in place since February 2025 and continues through the 2025-2026 review cycles. For more detailed information about the specific scoring descriptions for each point on the scale (1-5), you would need to access the actual review form at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c37caaf9-7598-4fc8-9bcc-d45cab0964b7","uuid":"02ae05cb-8b12-45cf-bd08-db1cd16b2dba","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:37:42.642Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form overall assessment scoring 1 2 3 4 5 scale 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Grdca7teqEMgnMTsq1U4dp","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"I found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review assessment scoring. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Review Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Overall Assessment Scale\n\nBased on the search results, the ACL Rolling Review uses a **1-5 scale** for the overall assessment scoring. The Overall Assessment descriptions include: 5.0 \"Award-worthy (top 2.5%)\" and 4.0 (the results appear to be truncated, but indicate there is a five-point scale).\n\n## Key Requirements\n\n- The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n- If you give a low Soundness score without finding any major faults, this means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation, and you need to revise it.\n\nThe search results show that this scoring system has been in place since February 2025 and continues through the 2025-2026 review cycles. For more detailed information about the specific scoring descriptions for each point on the scale (1-5), you would need to access the actual review form at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform."],"durationSeconds":5.798168846}}
